IMPORT prelude

-- National Council of Social Service Act 1992 (Singapore) -- who may be a sector member of the Council and how a refused or
-- revoked organisation appeals to the Minister (ss 15, 16); who may sit on the Council and the Community Chest (ss 5, 5B, 5F, 5G,
-- 5J, 13(4)-(6)); how the Council decides (ss 7, 9); and what reserves fall into the Endowment Fund (s 26(1)(b)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition (incorporating amendments to 1 December 2021), informal consolidation -- version in force from
-- 1 August 2026, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/NCSSA1992.txt. The latest amendment annotated is Act 3 of 2026
-- (wef 01/08/2026), which rewrote most of the Act. The ARRANGEMENT OF SECTIONS at the top of the deposit is out of step with the
-- body (it lists "11. Community Chest" and blank entries for 14 and 14A); this encoding follows the BODY, where s 11 is
-- objectives and functions, s 12 powers, s 13 the Community Chest, s 14 committees and s 14A delegation.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0189 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has
-- asked a sharper question yet. The Act is mostly the constitution of a statutory board; the part an outside organisation
-- actually meets is sector membership and its appeal, and the part an individual meets is eligibility to serve. SCOPED to those,
-- with the Council's quorum, voting and composition arithmetic.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: objectives, functions and powers (ss 11, 12); committees and delegation (ss 14, 14A); patrons (s 21); staff
-- (ss 22, 23); the financial provisions other than s 26(1)(b) (financial year, bank accounts, investment, borrowing, shares,
-- the 30 June and 30 September statement deadlines, ss 24-33); Ministerial directions (s 10); protection from liability (s 36);
-- regulation-making (ss 37, 38). No regulations under s 37 or s 38 were retrieved, so the "prescribed" standards for sector
-- members (s 15(4)) and the nomination criteria (s 5(3)) are not encoded.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `National Council of Social Service Act 1992 -- sector members, membership and decisions`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the larger of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `15 -- sector members`

-- s 15(1): "The Council may appoint an organisation to be a sector member of the Council." (3): "To be appointed as a sector
-- member, an organisation must either -- (a) have the primary function of providing a social service in Singapore; or (b) have
-- the primary function of directly supporting the provision of a social service in Singapore."
-- (4): a sector member "must comply with" prescribed standards of management, administration and service, and of cooperation
-- with the Council. (6): in appointing, re-appointing or revoking, the Council "may consider the organisation's aims, objects and
-- activities, including whether [they] are contrary to the public interest, public order or national harmony".
-- (7): sector members "are not members of the Council".
--
-- s 15(3) is a threshold only: an eligible organisation has no right to be appointed ("may appoint"). The rule below says only
-- whether the organisation clears the threshold.
GIVEN `provides a social service in Singapore as its primary function` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `directly supports a social service in Singapore as its primary function` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the organisation is eligible to be a sector member` IF
        `provides a social service in Singapore as its primary function`
    OR  `directly supports a social service in Singapore as its primary function`

§§ `16 -- appeal to the Minister`

-- s 16(1): "An organisation aggrieved by a decision mentioned in subsection (2) may appeal to the Minister within 14 days after
-- notice of the decision is served on the organisation or such extended period as the Minister may allow in any particular case."
-- (2): a decision of the Council "(a) refusing to appoint ...; (b) refusing to re-appoint ...; or (c) revoking that
-- organisation's appointment as a sector member".
--
-- s 37(2)(d) lets regulations provide for "sanctions ... including the issuance of letters of censure and the suspension or
-- revocation of appointment as a sector member". Of those, only revocation is listed in s 16(2). Whether the regulations give
-- their own appeal against censure or suspension was not checked (none were retrieved).
DECLARE Decision IS ONE OF
    `a refusal to appoint as a sector member`
    `a refusal to re-appoint as a sector member`
    `a revocation of sector membership`
    `a suspension of sector membership`
    `a letter of censure`

GIVEN `the decision` IS A Decision
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the decision can be appealed to the Minister` IF
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `a refusal to appoint as a sector member` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a refusal to re-appoint as a sector member` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a revocation of sector membership` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Days are counted from service of notice of the decision. `extended period allowed` is 0 where the Minister allowed none.
GIVEN `days after service of notice` IS A NUMBER, `extended period allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appeal is in time` IF
        `days after service of notice` AT MOST 14
    OR  `days after service of notice` AT MOST `extended period allowed`

-- s 16(3): the appellant must (a) "state as concisely as possible the circumstances ... and the issues and grounds" and (b)
-- submit it "together with all relevant facts, evidence and arguments" within the period. (4): the Minister may require
-- information or documents. (5): "The Minister is not under any duty to hear, consider or determine any appeal if -- (a) the
-- appellant does not comply with subsection (3) or (4); or (b) ... the appeal is or the proceedings ... are frivolous or
-- vexatious."
GIVEN `stated grounds and submitted the evidence in time` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `provided what the Minister required` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the appeal is frivolous or vexatious` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may decline to determine the appeal` IF
        (NOT `stated grounds and submitted the evidence in time`)
    OR  (NOT `provided what the Minister required`)
    OR  `the appeal is frivolous or vexatious`

-- s 16(6): "The decision appealed against must be complied with until the determination of the appeal unless otherwise directed
-- by the Minister in any particular case." An appeal does not suspend a revocation.
GIVEN `the Minister directed otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the decision binds while the appeal is pending` IF
    NOT `the Minister directed otherwise`

-- s 16(7): the Minister may determine an appeal by "(a) confirming, varying or cancelling the decision ...; or (b) directing the
-- Council to reconsider the decision". (8): "The decision of the Minister in any appeal is final."
DECLARE Outcome IS ONE OF
    `confirming the decision`
    `varying the decision`
    `cancelling the decision`
    `directing the Council to reconsider`
    `awarding damages to the organisation`

GIVEN `the outcome` IS A Outcome
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may determine the appeal by` IF
    CONSIDER `the outcome`
    WHEN `awarding damages to the organisation` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 16(10): the Minister may designate "(a) any Minister assigned by the Prime Minister to assist the Minister; (b) any Minister
-- of State; (c) any Parliamentary Secretary" to hear and determine an appeal in the Minister's place. A civil servant is not
-- on the list.
DECLARE OfficeHolder IS ONE OF
    `a Minister assigned to assist the Minister`
    `a Minister of State`
    `a Parliamentary Secretary`
    `the Permanent Secretary`
    `the Chief Executive Officer of the Council`

GIVEN `the office-holder` IS A OfficeHolder
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the office-holder may be designated to hear the appeal` IF
    CONSIDER `the office-holder`
    WHEN `a Minister assigned to assist the Minister` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a Minister of State` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a Parliamentary Secretary` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `5B -- who is disqualified from the Council`

-- s 5B(2): disqualified "to be or from being a member of the Council mentioned in section 5(2)(a), (d) or (e)":
--   (a) "an employee of the Council (other than the Chief Executive Officer)"; (b) "a Judge or judicial officer";
--   (c) "an undischarged bankrupt or an individual who has an arrangement with any of his or her creditors";
--   (d) convicted of "an offence involving dishonesty, fraud or moral turpitude and has not received a free pardon";
--   (e) "sentenced to imprisonment for a term of 6 months or more, and has not received a free pardon";
--   (f) disqualified as a company or VCC director under the Companies Act 1967 or the Variable Capital Companies Act 2018;
--   (g) lacks capacity within the Mental Capacity Act 2008, or is subject to an order under s 10 of the Mental Health (Care and
--       Treatment) Act 2008.
-- The free pardon in (d) and (e) is modelled as one flag covering whichever conviction or sentence is in question.
DECLARE Candidate HAS
    `is an employee of the Council` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is the Chief Executive Officer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a Judge or judicial officer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an undischarged bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has an arrangement with creditors` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was convicted of an offence of dishonesty, fraud or moral turpitude` IS A BOOLEAN
    `months of imprisonment sentenced` IS A NUMBER
    `received a free pardon` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is disqualified as a company or VCC director` IS A BOOLEAN
    `lacks capacity` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the candidate` IS A Candidate
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the candidate is disqualified from the Council` IF
        (`the candidate`'s `is an employee of the Council` AND (NOT `the candidate`'s `is the Chief Executive Officer`))
    OR  `the candidate`'s `is a Judge or judicial officer`
    OR  `the candidate`'s `is an undischarged bankrupt`
    OR  `the candidate`'s `has an arrangement with creditors`
    OR  (`the candidate`'s `was convicted of an offence of dishonesty, fraud or moral turpitude` AND (NOT `the candidate`'s `received a free pardon`))
    OR  (`the candidate`'s `months of imprisonment sentenced` AT LEAST 6 AND (NOT `the candidate`'s `received a free pardon`))
    OR  `the candidate`'s `is disqualified as a company or VCC director`
    OR  `the candidate`'s `lacks capacity`

§§ `13(4)-(6) -- who may sit on the Community Chest`

-- s 13(4): "Subject to subsection (5), an individual is disqualified to be or from being the chairperson, the deputy chairperson
-- or any other member of the Community Chest if he or she would be disqualified ... under section 5B(2)." (5): "The Chief
-- Executive Officer may be a member of the Community Chest but is not to be appointed as the chairperson or deputy chairperson".
-- (6): no appointment "unless, before appointment, he or she discloses to the Council the details of any interest".
DECLARE ChestRole IS ONE OF
    `chairperson of the Community Chest`
    `deputy chairperson of the Community Chest`
    `ordinary member of the Community Chest`

GIVEN `the candidate` IS A Candidate, `the role` IS A ChestRole, `disclosed interests to the Council beforehand` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the candidate may be appointed to the Community Chest` IF
        (NOT `the candidate is disqualified from the Council` `the candidate`)
    AND `disclosed interests to the Council beforehand`
    AND (    (NOT `the candidate`'s `is the Chief Executive Officer`)
         OR  CONSIDER `the role`
             WHEN `ordinary member of the Community Chest` THEN TRUE
             OTHERWISE FALSE)

§§ `5, 5A, 5F, 5G -- kinds of member, removal and resignation`

-- s 5(2): the members are (a) a Chairperson appointed by the Minister; (b) the Chief Executive Officer; (c) the chairperson of the
-- Community Chest; (d) at least 7 members appointed by the Minister "from a list of nominees to be submitted by the
-- Chairperson" (nominated by sector members, s 5(3)); (e) any number of other members appointed by the Minister.
-- s 5A(2)(a): the instrument of appointment states the term, "which must not be longer than 3 years" -- for (a), (d), (e) only.
-- s 5F(1): "The Minister may, at any time and without giving any reason, remove a member ... mentioned in section 5(2)(a), (d)
-- or (e)". s 5G(1): a member "(other than the Chief Executive Officer or the chairperson of the Community Chest) may resign".
-- The CEO and the Community Chest chairperson sit by virtue of another office, so none of these apply to them.
DECLARE MemberKind IS ONE OF
    `the Chairperson`
    `the Chief Executive Officer as member`
    `the chairperson of the Community Chest as member`
    `a member nominated through sector members`
    `another member appointed by the Minister`

GIVEN `the kind` IS A MemberKind
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the member holds an appointment the Minister may end without reason` IF
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `the Chief Executive Officer as member` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the chairperson of the Community Chest as member` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the kind` IS A MemberKind
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the member may resign from the Council by notice to the Minister` IF
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `the Chief Executive Officer as member` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the chairperson of the Community Chest as member` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `5(1), (4) -- composition of the Council`

-- s 5(1): "The Council consists of at least 15 but not more than 27 members." (2)(d): "at least 7" nominated members.
-- (4): "The number of members appointed under subsection (2)(d) must be at least half of the total number of members, excluding
-- the Chairperson." The CEO and the Community Chest chairperson count in that total; the Chairperson does not.
GIVEN `total members` IS A NUMBER, `nominated members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Council is lawfully composed` IF
        `total members` AT LEAST 15
    AND `total members` AT MOST 27
    AND `nominated members` AT LEAST 7
    AND `nominated members` TIMES 2 AT LEAST `total members` MINUS 1

§§ `7 -- quorum`

-- s 7(1): "The quorum for a meeting of the Council is the higher of the following: (a) one-third of the number of members;
-- (b) 7 members." (2): "No business may be transacted at a meeting of the Council if a quorum is not present."
-- "one-third" of a number not divisible by 3 is read as a floor that must be reached (25 members: 8 present is below 8 1/3).
-- That reading is an inference; the text does not say how to round.
GIVEN `members of the Council` IS A NUMBER, `members present` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a quorum is present` IF
        `members present` TIMES 3 AT LEAST `members of the Council`
    AND `members present` AT LEAST 7

§§ `9 -- voting`

-- s 9(1): "Each member of the Council has one vote." (2): the presiding member has, "in the case of an equality of votes, a
-- casting vote". (3): a resolution passes "if it is agreed to by all members present without dissent, or if a majority of the
-- votes cast on it by members present and voting are in favour of it". (4): a member present "is presumed to have agreed to,
-- and to have cast a vote in favour of, a decision ... unless the member expressly dissents from or votes against the decision
-- at the meeting or is prevented from voting by section 26 of the Public Sector (Governance) Act 2018".
--
-- Read together (an inference from s 9(4)): every member present who neither dissents nor is barred counts as a vote FOR.
-- There is no abstention.
GIVEN `members present at the vote` IS A NUMBER,
      `members who dissent or vote against` IS A NUMBER,
      `members barred from voting` IS A NUMBER,
      `the presiding member casts for` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the resolution is passed` IF
        `members present at the vote` MINUS `members who dissent or vote against` MINUS `members barred from voting`
            GREATER THAN `members who dissent or vote against`
    OR  (    `members present at the vote` MINUS `members who dissent or vote against` MINUS `members barred from voting`
                 EQUALS `members who dissent or vote against`
         AND `the presiding member casts for`)

§§ `5J(1)(g) -- absence from meetings`

-- s 5J(1): a member "ceases to hold office if he or she -- ... (g) fails to attend 3 consecutive meetings of the Council without
-- the approval of the Council". The other grounds (death, bankruptcy, disqualification, removal, resignation, undisclosed interest
-- notified to the Minister, non-reappointment) are collapsed into one flag. (2): no "compensation or other payment or benefit"
-- on ceasing to hold office "for any reason".
GIVEN `consecutive meetings missed without approval` IS A NUMBER, `another ground in s 5J(1) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the member ceases to hold office` IF
        `consecutive meetings missed without approval` AT LEAST 3
    OR  `another ground in s 5J(1) applies`

§§ `26(1)(b) -- reserves swept into the Endowment Fund`

-- s 26(1): the Endowment Fund consists of "(a) all donations and gifts accepted by the Council for the Endowment Fund; (b) all
-- reserves of the Council in excess of 2 years of its operating expenditure; and (c) any other moneys that the Council decides to
-- transfer". (3): the Fund "may be applied for such purposes as may be approved by the Minister in writing".
-- "2 years of its operating expenditure" is read as twice an annual operating expenditure figure (an inference; the Act does not
-- say which years).
GIVEN `reserves` IS A NUMBER, `annual operating expenditure` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the reserves in the Endowment Fund under s 26(1)(b)` MEANS
    `the larger of` (`reserves` MINUS (2 TIMES `annual operating expenditure`)) 0
